1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,976
Valentine's Day. One nice dinner. How much could it cost?

2
00:00:04,396 --> 00:00:07,968
Let's add up the real number, then build a version that fits your plan.

3
00:00:08,388 --> 00:00:09,215
Here's the dinner.

4
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:10,955
Two entrées, $76.

5
00:00:11,115 --> 00:00:12,781
Appetizer and dessert, $30.

6
00:00:12,941 --> 00:00:14,306
Four drinks, $48.

7
00:00:14,466 --> 00:00:15,334
Tax, $12.

8
00:00:15,494 --> 00:00:17,383
And a 20% tip, $31.

9
00:00:17,803 --> 00:00:20,139
That's $197, before anything else.

10
00:00:20,559 --> 00:00:25,382
Add flowers, $65. A gift, $75. And rides there and back, $30.

11
00:00:26,152 --> 00:00:32,277
In our example budget, fun money is $100 a paycheck. That one night is almost four paychecks of it.

12
00:00:32,697 --> 00:00:35,518
So here are two ways to do it without wrecking February.

13
00:00:36,288 --> 00:00:38,164
Option one. The planned night in.

14
00:00:38,584 --> 00:00:40,119
Here's a hundred dollar version.

15
00:00:40,279 --> 00:00:42,781
Groceries for a really nice dinner, $48.

16
00:00:42,941 --> 00:00:44,489
A bottle of wine, $18.

17
00:00:44,649 --> 00:00:46,542
Grocery-store flowers, $15.

18
00:00:46,702 --> 00:00:48,081
Dessert to share, $12.

19
00:00:48,241 --> 00:00:53,405
And a printed photo with a handwritten card, $7. Often the part people remember most.

20
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:59,028
$100. One paycheck of fun money. $267 less than the night out.

21
00:00:59,798 --> 00:01:01,847
Option two. Splurge on purpose.

22
00:01:02,267 --> 00:01:11,281
The night out isn't wrong. Unplanned is the problem. If you love it, plan for it: $367 over 26 paychecks is $15 each.

23
00:01:11,701 --> 00:01:16,981
Start a sinking fund now, and next February is already paid for. Episode three shows how.

24
00:01:17,401 --> 00:01:20,328
Either way, decide the number before you're sitting at the table.

25
00:01:21,098 --> 00:01:26,434
The Paycheck Planner in the description has a surprise fund tab for exactly this kind of plan.

26
00:01:26,854 --> 00:01:31,299
Subscribe. Next time: tax refund advances, and what they really cost.
